# Keep host build artefacts out of the SCORED build context.
#
# `git` ignoring a file is NOT the same as `docker` ignoring it. This folder IS
# the build context, and the Dockerfile's `COPY . /src` copies whatever is on
# disk. A local `sh build.sh` leaves `run` behind, and rustc on Windows also
# writes `run.pdb`; if the in-image compile ever failed to replace `run` -- or
# produced it under a different name -- then `COPY --from=build /src/run
# /app/run` would ship a stale host binary of unknown provenance to the scoring
# box. `.gitignore` only stops the COMMIT, never the CONTEXT, and every
# tracked-file audit stays green while it happens.
#
# These rules do not affect the build itself: `RUN ./build.sh` creates /src/run
# *inside* the build stage, and .dockerignore is applied only to the context
# upload, so the freshly compiled binary is what gets copied to the runtime
# stage. Every name below is asserted by tooling/check-track-folders.sh, which
# fails if a forbidden file sits in this folder without a matching line here.
run
run.exe
run.pdb
*.pdb
*.exe
*.o
*.rlib
*.log
*.tmp